@startuml fig-S09-e3-states
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

title S09 — Tunnel Frame: Explicit Wire Order

class "TNL1 frame (offsets in bytes)" as wire #F5F5F5 {
  0..3: Magic = ASCII TNL1 (4 bytes)
  4: Type = O / D / C / E (uint8)
  5..6: Session ID (uint16, big-endian)
  7: Service ID (uint8)
  8..11: Payload Length N (uint32, big-endian)
  12..(11+N): Payload (N bytes)
}

note right of wire
  Read the fixed 12-byte header first,
  then exactly N payload bytes.
  Reject N above the configured maximum.
  Empty payload: N=0, frame ends at offset 11.
end note

legend bottom
  Wire order is top to bottom, by increasing byte offset.
  O = OPEN, D = DATA, C = CLOSE, E = ERROR.
  Session ID identifies an interleaved tunnel session.
  Service ID maps to an internal backend in YAML configuration.
endlegend
@enduml
